I'm Olivier, and I'm Mauritian. West of Mauritius is my guide to one stretch of coast: from [Flic en Flac](/en/areas/flic-en-flac) in the north to [Le Morne](/en/areas/le-morne) in the south, and up into the hills of [Chamarel](/en/areas/chamarel). It is written for people who come to visit, and for people thinking of making a home here.

## How I work

- **Facts are checked.** Heights, dates, distances, rules and prices are checked against reliable sources, and every guide lists its sources at the end with the date I checked them.
- **Nothing is invented.** No made up reviews, ratings, prices or opening hours. Where something changes often, I say so and tell you to check before you go.
- **Nothing paid for is hidden.** Featured places and partner links are labelled on the page, and they never change what I write.
- **Pages are kept up to date.** Every guide shows when it was last updated.

## Where to start

- [The six areas](/en/areas), from Flic en Flac to Chamarel.
- [Guides](/en/guides) to the beaches, sunsets, hikes and practical matters.
- [Living in the West](/en/living-in-the-west), if you are thinking of moving here or buying a home.

## Get in touch

Spotted something wrong or out of date, or know a place I should see? Write to me through the [contact page](/en/contact), or join the [west coast community](/en/community).
